meta {
  name: Get Performance (This Month)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/performance?range=mtd
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  range: mtd
  ~from: 2026-01-01
  ~to: 2026-01-31
  ~scope: own
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("echoes the resolved window back", function () {
    const range = res.getBody().range;
    expect(range.key).to.equal("mtd");
    expect(range.from).to.match(/^\d{4}-\d{2}-01$/);
    expect(range.to).to.match(/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/);
  });

  test("returns both cards", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("sold");
    expect(body).to.have.property("quoted");
  });

  test("averages are a number or null, never NaN", function () {
    // The contract the UI depends on: `null` means "no households to divide
    // by", which renders as an em dash rather than as $0.
    const body = res.getBody();
    for (const card of [body.sold, body.quoted]) {
      for (const key of ["avgPremiumPerHousehold", "avgItemsPerHousehold"]) {
        const value = card[key];
        expect(value === null || typeof value === "number").to.equal(true);
        if (value !== null) expect(Number.isNaN(value)).to.equal(false);
      }
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /performance — Sold + Quoted scorecards (PAC-10 / PAC-11)

  Both Producer Dashboard scorecards in one request. They always show the same
  window, so splitting them would let the two halves of a single visual row
  disagree mid-refresh.

  - **Module:** `performance` (must be enabled for the agency)
  - **Permission:** `performance:read`
  - **Read-only** — there is no mutating handler. A scorecard is a projection of
    `deals` and `quoteRecaps`, so `PATCH /performance` is a `404`.
  - **Data scope** (enforced in the service layer):
    - `own` → only the caller's own rows (`producerId = user`)
    - `branch` → rows in the caller's branch (or the `X-Branch-Id` branch)
    - `agency` → all rows in the agency

  ## Query params
  | param | type | default | rules |
  |-------|------|---------|-------|
  | range | enum | `mtd`   | `today` \| `week` \| `mtd` \| `lastMonth` \| `custom` |
  | from  | date | —       | `YYYY-MM-DD`. **Required** when `range=custom` |
  | to    | date | —       | `YYYY-MM-DD`, **inclusive**. Required when `range=custom` |
  | scope | enum | —       | `own` \| `agency`. A *request*, clamped to the caller's `DataScope` — it can only ever narrow |

  ### Windows
  All boundaries are **America/Chicago calendar days**, compared as `YYYYMMDD`
  integers against the indexed `deals.soldDateYmd` / `quoteRecaps.quoteDateYmd`.

  | range | window |
  |-------|--------|
  | `today` | today |
  | `week` | the trailing **7 days including today** — not a calendar week |
  | `mtd` | 1st of this month → **today** (not month end: a producer can type a future sold date) |
  | `lastMonth` | the whole previous calendar month |
  | `custom` | `from` → `to`, both inclusive, max **366 days** |

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "range": { "key": "mtd", "from": "2026-08-01", "to": "2026-08-06" },
    "sold": {
      "premium": 31662,
      "itemCount": 27,
      "recordCount": 11,
      "householdCount": 8,
      "avgPremiumPerHousehold": 3957.75,
      "avgItemsPerHousehold": 3.38
    },
    "quoted": { "…": "same shape" }
  }
  ```

  | field | type | notes |
  |-------|------|-------|
  | premium | number | summed, rounded to cents |
  | itemCount | number | **items**, not records — a deal with three policies counts three |
  | recordCount | number | matching documents; exposed so the averages are auditable |
  | householdCount | number | **distinct** households across those documents |
  | avgPremiumPerHousehold | number \| null | `null` — never `0` — when `householdCount` is 0 |
  | avgItemsPerHousehold | number \| null | same |

  ### The household denominator
  Net-new: legacy had no per-household metric at all. A row's household identity
  is resolved through a fallback ladder — `householdId`, else
  `legacyHouseholdId`, else **the row's own id**, meaning an unattributed row
  counts as its own household. That can only *understate* the average, and it
  converges on the true value as `npm run backfill:deal-refs:dev` fills the refs
  in. Collapsing null-household rows into one bucket would inflate it without
  bound on migrated data.

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — `range=custom` without both bounds, `from` after `to`, a
    date that does not exist (`2026-02-31`), a span over 366 days, or an unknown
    `range` value.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `performance` module disabled, or missing
    `performance:read`.

  > **Tip:** log in as `producer@smithfamily.local` — the demo seed makes them
  > the data-rich producer for this dashboard.
}
